---
// "Direct Rescue" before/after mockup — the counter to a generic-analytics "Unknown source"
// row. GTM doc §4 Tier 1 / §8 ("Without/With" demo countering Unknown→ChatGPT).
//
// ── WHAT THIS IS, AND THE LINE IT DOES NOT CROSS (§6, §29.5) ─────────────────────────
// STATIC FIXTURE MARKUP. No network call, no data client, no query helper, no real customer
// data — same construction as DashboardMockup.astro and JourneyMockup.astro, and the same
// rule §29.5 sets for the public demo. The card carries its own "Sample data" badge.
// (The guard test greps this whole FILE for data-access tokens, comments included, so that a
// commented-out call is caught too — which is why none are spelled out literally here.)
//
// It depicts what SourceTrack's own REPORTING shows: an AI referrer that generic analytics
// records as Direct is attributed to ChatGPT. That claim is true today — AI-source detection
// is shipped and its read endpoints are live.
//
// It deliberately does NOT depict the unbuilt half of GTM §4 Tier 1: injecting a synthetic
// `utm_source=chatgpt` into a hidden form field so the customer's CRM record changes. That
// is real tracker + form-layer work with DNT/GPC gating implications, and it does not exist.
// So there is no CRM in this mockup, no hidden-field illustration, and no copy implying a
// lead's record in another system is rewritten. Depicting it would make this a claim about
// live behaviour rather than a demo — the §6 violation this whole component is built to
// avoid. If that capability ships, this mockup may be extended; until then it must not
// anticipate it.
//
// ── The left card is DELIBERATELY GENERIC ────────────────────────────────────────────
// No competitor name, no competitor logo, no competitor screenshot — per design.md §35.3,
// competitor brand assets are a trademark constraint, not a style preference. "Most
// analytics tools" is a category statement, which is defensible; a named tool's UI is not
// ours to draw.

// Fixture rows. Same lead, two views of it. Illustrative only.
const lead = {
  page: "/pricing",
  when: "Today, 14:32",
  value: "$2,000",
};
---

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[880px]">
  <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr] md:items-center">
    <!-- BEFORE — generic analytics. Muted on purpose: this is the state being escaped. -->
    <div class="rounded-[24px] border border-[#2D3333] bg-[#121616] p-4">
      <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-[11px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9DA7A7]">
          Most analytics tools
        </span>
        <span
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-white/5 px-2.5 py-1 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9DA7A7]"
        >
          Sample data
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#2D3333] bg-[#181D1D] p-4">
        <div class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9DA7A7]">Source</div>
        <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#6B7676]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="text-xl font-black tracking-tight text-[#9DA7A7]">Direct / Unknown</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div>
            <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7676]">Landing page</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-[#C7CFCF]">{lead.page}</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7676]">Value</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-[#C7CFCF]">{lead.value}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#9DA7A7]">
        No referrer to read, so the visit lands in a catch-all bucket. The channel that actually
        produced it is not recorded.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Arrow. Rotates to point down when the cards stack on mobile. -->
    <div class="flex items-center justify-center md:px-1" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg
        class="h-6 w-6 rotate-90 text-primary md:rotate-0"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
      >
        <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- AFTER — SourceTrack. The same lead, attributed. -->
    <div class="relative rounded-[24px] border border-primary/25 bg-[#121616] p-4">
      <div
        class="absolute -right-4 -top-6 h-[140px] w-[140px] rounded-full bg-primary opacity-[0.18] blur-[42px]"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
      </div>

      <div class="relative mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-[11px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#F5F8F8]">
          SourceTrack
        </span>
        <span
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
        >
          Sample data
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="relative rounded-2xl border border-primary/20 bg-[#181D1D] p-4">
        <div class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9DA7A7]">Source</div>
        <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="text-xl font-black tracking-tight text-white">ChatGPT</span>
          <span
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-white/5 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#C7CFCF]"
          >
            AI Search
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div>
            <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7676]">Landing page</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-[#C7CFCF]">{lead.page}</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7676]">Value</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-white">{lead.value}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="relative mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#C7CFCF]">
        The AI referrer is recognised, so the visit is reported against the channel that produced
        it instead of a catch-all.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-5 text-center text-xs text-gray">
    Illustrative example, not a customer's data. It shows how the same visit is reported in
    SourceTrack.
  </p>
</div>
